id: pm-vcs-rmqh
title: Research Epic Lore and map its general-VCS design into pm-vcs
description: "Study EpicGames/lore from its canonical repository and first-party specification, distinguish it from the kernel lore patch-series workflow, and turn the findings into a capability-by-capability pm-vcs design map covering arbitrary files, binary-first storage, file identity, sparse/lazy working copies, remotes, locking, multi-tenancy, links/layers, lifecycle deletion, APIs, and PM-linked file attribution."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: architecture,"area:vcs",lore,research,roadmap
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:24:45.241Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T22:05:58.026Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T19:40:23.218Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T19:40:23.218Z"
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: The PM item body cites Epic canonical Lore sources; pm-vcs shipped state and roadmap gaps are explicit; kernel lore and Epic Lore are no longer conflated in PM records; PM-linked file-change attribution has a concrete native design and acceptance boundary; Every relevant Lore capability is classified as retain adopt adapt reject or defer
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
resolution: "Researched Epic Lore canonical sources; published the detailed capability map in LORE.md and PM; expanded Phases 3, 5 and 6; created four non-duplicated implementation features; and reconciled the research record after stable FileId attribution shipped."
expected_result: Detailed first-party Lore research and an actionable general-VCS roadmap exist in linked package documentation and durable pm-vcs PM records.
actual_result: "LORE.md and pm-vcs-rmqh contain the source-linked research; pm-vcs-ag8y shipped stable FileId attribution; pm-vcs-vmmx, pm-vcs-0lec and pm-vcs-8xis retain the fragment, sparse-instance, composition and lifecycle roadmap."
